In .NET MAUI, the `Application` class no longer has `OnStart`, `OnSleep`, and `OnResume` virtual methods. Instead, use the **lifecycle events** via `Window`:

```csharp
public partial class App : Application
{
    protected override Window CreateWindow(IActivationState? activationState)
    {
        var window = new Window(new MainPage());

        window.Created += (s, e) => { /* replaces OnStart */ };
        window.Stopped += (s, e) => { /* replaces OnSleep */ };
        window.Resumed += (s, e) => { /* replaces OnResume */ };

        return window;
    }
}
```

**Key differences:**
- Lifecycle is now per-**window**, not per-app (MAUI supports multi-window).
- Additional events available: `Activated`, `Deactivated`, `Destroying`, `Backgrounding`.
- For platform-specific hooks, you can also use `ConfigureLifecycleEvents` in `MauiProgram.cs`.
